<title>SOUTH AFRICA: CMH yr shr falls, looks to lift 97/98 shr.</title>
<headline>CMH yr shr falls, looks to lift 97/98 shr.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended February 28</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     75.2	  vs 99.4</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 28.0	  vs 28.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   14.80	 vs 19.58</p>
<p>    Operating income	29.91	 vs 42.50</p>
<p>    Tax			 9.82	  vs 13.68</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   6.49	  vs 11.25</p>
<p>    Turnover		  1,051.95    vs 1,0217.72</p>
<p>Div payable June 13</p>
<p>on register May 9</p>
<p>Full name: Combined Motor Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said the sound balance sheet of the group, which serves all major segments of the vehicle market, coupled with a strong and capable management team will provide the platform for increased earnings in the new financial year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
